  "repairs": [
    "Fresh SUM0 objects have an explicit constructor variant; equal distinct objects and builtin singleton identity remain distinct.",
    "Aggregate calls retain grouping sets, direct-argument counts, input fields, filter, distinct keys, ordering, flags, type, name and parser coordinates.",
    "Window descriptors retain partition keys, orderings, bounds, exclusions and call counts; Uncollect retains independent passthrough and expansion mappings, including valid overlap.",
    "Trait alternatives preserve Calcite ordering, including its field-ordinal-only collation comparison. Metadata reconstruction checks exact traits and hints, quoting, positions and UTF-8-sorted map keys.",
    "Rust validates metadata field bounds against producer rows and bounds cumulative entry, reference and string work. Unknown variants, missing fields and invalid references fail."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Expression slot counts are descriptors, not global expression IDs. Full call/lambda/correlation/source-use transport and descriptor-to-expression linkage remain open.",
    "Names identify scans for this audit, not full catalog objects. Full statements, declarations, catalog identity, JDBC convention and general transient traits need adapters.",
    "The corpus contains fifteen relation forms; JDBC scans and LogicalCorrelate are absent. No corpus coverage is inferred for absent forms.",
    "Java reconstructs aggregate operator objects, traits and hints, not complete RelNodes or aggregate-call expression arguments. System-field names and indices need the complete relation adapter.",
    "Full detached S1-to-S2 and P0 remain incomplete."
  ]
}
